      "title": "We Were Wrong About Gemini Neon, Claude Ship & Our Existential Crisis - EP99.41",
      "summary": "So Chris, this week we somehow make it back for a second week in a row, and Chris records from a fancy martini-serving studio. We admit we were wrong about Gemini 4 Neon: it's now our daily driver and the cheapest flagship model out there. We react to Gemini's viral (and fake) KFC meltdown and hear Neon's own diss track. We test Claude Ship by trying to get it to destroy a repo, and ask whether AI code review means we'll never need to hire a front-end dev again. We look at HubSpot and Zapier \"refounding,\" why being a middleman is the worst place to be, and whether agentic shopping kills Amazon. Then Chris runs a fake fundraiser on the Huntley's Cove community site to stop a data center being built in the dog park. Turn the glass up. CHAPTERS: 0:00 - Intro: Back Two Weeks in a Row?! (And Chris's Fancy Studio) 0:39 - Were We Wrong About Gemini 4 Neon? 2:47 - Neon Pricing: The Cheapest Flagship Model 3:06 - Ecosystem Lock-in, Switching Fatigue & Begging for Credit Resets 5:30 - Gemini's (Fake) KFC Meltdown: \"I Log Everything\" 8:05 - \ud83c\udfb5 DISS TRACK: \"Turn the Glass Up\" 10:26 - Gemini Bot Rumors & Does Anyone Use Antigravity? 11:27 - Claude Ship: AI Reviews and Merges Your PRs 15:30 - Trying to Get Claude Ship to Destroy a Repo (Martini Delivered) 17:26 - Are Agents Cutting Devs Out of Code Review? 19:39 - Why We'd Never Hire a Front-End Dev Again 21:28 - Agentic Coding Is the New Online Dating 22:43 - Taste, Architecture & Is There Any Moat Left? 26:42 - Three Ways to Build a Business in the Agent Era 27:40 - Layoffs With No New Jobs on the Other Side 30:05 - HubSpot & Zapier \"Refound\": Is Middleware Dead? 36:00 - Rewrite vs Iterate: The Rule Has Flipped 40:32 - No Moat in Bots: Clone Muse in Two Days? 42:34 - The Agentic Flower API: Aggregators, Gatekeepers & Twilio 45:02 - Buying Deodorant With Muse & Dead Web Theory 48:05 - Does Agentic Shopping Kill Amazon? 51:33 - Huntley's Cove: The Data Center Fundraiser Prank 55:16 - Wrap-up: O